# ---- one identity per ticket (optional — ON is the default) ----
# A board ticket id may have ONE build identity. bin/run-build.sh refuses a
# launch (BUILD_DEFERRED, exit 3, re-offered next tick) when that ticket id
# already has a live, PR_CREATED or merged build under a DIFFERENT key — the
# case a decomposed child creates when it is launched under its `<PARENT>.<n>`
# title label instead of the board's own key. The check is
# bin/lib/ticket-identity.sh and it runs before the Fly enqueue, the slot lock
# and the queue claim, so a refusal costs one API read and no model tokens.
# Refusal needs evidence: an unreachable ledger with nothing local proceeds and
# says so in the build's pipeline.log.
#   1 = on (default)
#   0 = off: the guard logs one line and never refuses anything.
#TICKET_IDENTITY_GUARD=1

